WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.744
Feng Dao was a young and talented official, serving at the court of the first dynasty.

00:00:07.094 --> 00:00:11.390
Young as he was, he worked carefully and diligently.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:19.396
The court's banners changed again and again, yet he always sat at his desk, calmly handling government affairs.

00:00:19.746 --> 00:00:25.002
As the years passed and his beard gradually turned white, he still worked diligently every day.

00:00:25.352 --> 00:00:30.032
The candlelight on his desk kept him company through many nights.

00:00:30.382 --> 00:00:35.854
In his old age he called himself the 'Old Man of Everlasting Joy', quietly reading and writing in his garden.

00:00:36.204 --> 00:00:40.548
Butterflies danced in the garden, and his heart was completely at peace.

00:00:40.898 --> 00:00:46.154
Later generations judged him differently: some criticized him, others praised him.

00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:50.368
As the two scholars talked on, both gradually fell silent.

00:00:50.718 --> 00:00:57.030
But the books and classics he preserved became a precious cultural heritage.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:01.292
These books helped later generations understand that age.

